      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The current phrasing of Section 4(c) is a strategic misstep that needs immediate reframing for Senator Vance. We should pivot the discussion away from \"margin squeeze\" and instead emphasize how the tax credit structure, as written, provides a necessary *stabilizing floor* for domestic production during volatile market cycles. Frame it as a proactive measure that ensures long-term operational resilience for manufacturers, which directly aligns with his mandate to protect American industry. By focusing on stability over immediate profit, we keep him firmly in support of the legislation.",
